|~ What is declared under `::null`, the kind of the absent value: its
   constructor and its refusal, and the soft read of it, told in one
   order: the word and its page, its answer, its parts, its refusals,
   its laws. ~|

:null/construct
  |~~ Reads null as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:null/PayloadNotNullError
  |~~ `::null` reads its payload as null; a payload of another kind is
      refused.
  ~~|

:null/PayloadNotNullError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number payload is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(::null(1) !| [type /actualType] | eq [::null/PayloadNotNullError ::number])

:null/at
  |~~ Answers the default the call gives, null when it gives none,
      whatever the place: null holds nothing, so a soft read of it is
      absent, `null | at :k` answering `null` and `null | at :k "none"`
      answering `"none"`. So soft reads chain through what is absent,
      `at :address | at :city`, a step that misses answering null to the
      end, and a `coalesce` after them gives the fallback once, where
      the strict `/k` refuses null as it refuses every value without
      parts. The place is not read, so any value stands there.
      ::link~(::map/at | doc) ::link~(::vec/at | doc)
      ::link~(::any/coalesce | doc)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:null/at/answer
  |~~ The default, null when the call gives none. ~~|
  ::any

:null/at/place
  |~~ The place the call names, any value, unread: null holds none. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:null/at/default
  |~~ The value answered for a place the subject does not hold, null when it gives none. ~~|
  ~(at 1)

:null/at/readsNullFromNull
  |~~ A read of null answers null. ~~|
  ::law~(null | at :k | eq null)

:null/at/answersTheDefault
  |~~ A read of null answers the default the call gives. ~~|
  ::law~(null | at :k "none" | eq "none")

:null/at/chainsThroughAnAbsentValue
  |~~ Soft reads chain through an absent value. ~~|
  ::law~({:a null} | at :a | at :b | coalesce "none" | eq "none")

:null/at/chainsThroughPresentValues
  |~~ Soft reads chain through present values to the one read. ~~|
  ::law~({:a {:b 1}} | at :a | at :b | eq 1)

:null/at/readsNoPlace
  |~~ Any value stands as the place. ~~|
  ::law~(null | at [1 2] | eq null)
